[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:54. Sticky Fingers]
[00:00.260]Passage 54 | 文章五十四
[00:02.220]Sticky Fingers | 粘手
[00:05.250]After breakfast I sent the children to school, and then I went to market. | 早餐后我把孩子们送去学校，然后就去市场了。
[00:11.920]It was still early when I returned home. | 我回到家时还很早。
[00:15.420]The children were at school, my husband was at work, and the house was quiet. | 孩子们在学校，我丈夫在上班，家里一片宁静。
[00:22.045]So I decided to make some tarts for tea. | 于是我决定做些蛋挞当下午茶。
[00:26.265]In a short time I was busy mixing butter and flour, and my hands were soon covered with sticky pastry. | 不一会儿，我便忙着混合黄油和面粉，我的手很快就沾满了黏糊糊的糕点面团。
[00:34.545]At exactly that moment, the telephone rang. | 就在那一刻，电话铃响了。
[00:39.595]Nothing could have been more annoying. | 没有什么比这更烦人的了。
[00:42.625]I picked up the receiver between two sticky fingers, and was dismayed when I recognized the voice of Mrs. Bates. | 我用两根黏糊糊的手指拿起听筒，当我认出是贝茨太太的声音时，我感到很沮丧。
[00:51.625]It took me 10 minutes to persuade her to ring back later. | 我花了10分钟才说服她稍后再打回来。
[00:56.490]At last, I hung up the receiver. | 最后，我挂断了听筒。
[01:00.340]What a mess! | 真是一团糟！
[01:02.715]There was pastry on my fingers, on the telephone, and on the door knobs. | 我的手指上、电话上和门把手上都沾着糕点。
[01:09.150]I had no sooner got back to the kitchen than the doorbell rang loud enough to wake the dead. | 我刚回到厨房，门铃就响了，声音大到足以把死人吵醒。
[01:17.100]This time it was the postman, and he wanted me to sign for a registered letter. | 这次是邮递员，他要我签收一封挂号信。